/target
Cargo.lock
dist/

# crates/clean-signals-forgekit is a standalone package (its own [workspace]
# root outside the root workspace — see root Cargo.toml's exclude), so its build
# output lands in its own target/ dir rather than the root /target. Its
# Cargo.lock, by contrast, is committed (force-added past the global Cargo.lock
# ignore above) like a binary/leaf crate, since the crate pins a path dependency
# on a remote-less ForgeKit checkout.
/crates/clean-signals-forgekit/target
